this node will take in the following topics:
- /motion
- /pir_state

this node will then output data in the following format
- pir:x, rcwl:x

this will result in one of the following 4 conditions:
- pir:0, rcwl:0
- pir:1, rcwl:0
- pir:0, rcwl:1
- pir:1, rcwl:1

this data will be transmitted via the following topic:
- /fusedMotion

this topic will be consumed by the State_motion node


Create the node
- create the node using '01_SensorFusion_motion_node'
- add node to setup.py 'entry-points

BSR
- navigate to the workspace
- BUILD- colcon build
- SOURCE- source install/setup.bash
- RUN- pir node
- RUN- rcwl node
- RUN- SensorFusion_motion node

Verify Results
- open separate terminals for each node and use ros2 topic echo </topic name>
- the terminal windows should show correct and useful data for each of the individual topics as well as for the fused topic
